It seems a little artificial not to provide a complete status line by
the way.  That would let us know the player's experience level, stats,
burden status and AC.

The player's boots are water-walking, but other than the plus that
doesn't provide help in this situation.

The proper solution, I'd say, is to zap the monster with the wand of
slow monster right off.  Leocrottas are no joke for weak characters,
but the worst thing about them is their speed and multiple attacks.
The player has no means of escape other than to just climb out of the
pit (diagonally is best), and slow monster would give him extra turns
of survivability until that happens as well as allow him to get away
afterward assuming he's not burdened.

Once the monster is slow, the player can use the old Rogue tactic of
hitting the monster only when he has a spare move on it and run
otherwise.  Slowed monsters never recover from the slowing, so it gives
the player the best edge here, I'd say.

